1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,667
Most trading agents are built to trade.

2
00:00:02,667 --> 00:00:04,367
This one is built to refuse.

3
00:00:04,367 --> 00:00:09,200
Over the live week it evaluated 197 real opportunities and declined 98 percent of

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:09,533
them,

5
00:00:09,533 --> 00:00:13,300
and every refusal is a signed artifact you can verify yourself.

6
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:16,400
Let me show you why that is the point, not a bug.

7
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:19,300
The thesis is the volatility risk premium:

8
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:23,033
SPY options are priced richer than the movement that follows.

9
00:00:23,033 --> 00:00:27,400
Before a single line of backtest code, I pre-registered the hypotheses,

10
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:30,100
the trial count, and a multiple-testing bar.

11
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:32,300
The git history proves the order.

12
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:36,533
Nearly seven years of SPY, out of sample:

13
00:00:36,533 --> 00:00:43,633
mean premium 3.68 vol points over 1,741 observations, Newey-West t of 4.74.

14
00:00:43,633 --> 00:00:49,233
The naive t of 18 is invalid, because the windows overlap.

15
00:00:49,533 --> 00:00:53,700
The agent sells that premium with defined-risk iron condors,

16
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:59,500
only after eleven numbered gates pass: position integrity, timing, circuit breakers,

17
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:04,767
a contango filter, the premium threshold at the exact strikes it would sell,

18
00:01:04,767 --> 00:01:08,267
event proximity, cost, sizing, and a stagger rule.

19
00:01:08,267 --> 00:01:14,200
Every call goes through Alpaca's official MCP server, request and response recorded.

20
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:17,967
The deployed tenor was not picked from the backtest ranking.

21
00:01:17,967 --> 00:01:22,733
Since the twenty second of August three candidates have run as shadow agents on the

22
00:01:22,733 --> 00:01:24,733
same live prices, placing nothing.

23
00:01:24,733 --> 00:01:29,000
The deployed one would have entered on 26 cycles of 52, against 16 and 13.

24
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,067
The one that actually trades won.

25
00:01:31,367 --> 00:01:35,300
Every decision, fill and refusal is hashed into a Merkle tree,

26
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:37,433
sealed before outcomes are known.

27
00:01:37,433 --> 00:01:42,367
One command runs the tests, recomputes the root and rebuilds the results page.

28
00:01:42,367 --> 00:01:47,400
If anything had been edited after the fact, this line would not say verified.

29
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:50,433
Here is the strongest evidence that this works.

30
00:01:50,433 --> 00:01:54,700
On the first live morning, a payload-parsing bug read the account as flat,

31
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,633
and the agent stacked four condors instead of one.

32
00:01:57,633 --> 00:01:59,100
The sealed log caught it:

33
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:02,700
one artifact holds both the raw broker response with the legs,

34
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:05,100
and the reconciliation that ignored them.

35
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:09,433
Bug, fix, regression tests and the adopted positions are all in the record.

36
00:02:09,433 --> 00:02:10,500
I did not hide it.

37
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:12,300
The record would not let me.

38
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:16,600
This is an AI agents hackathon, so where does the model sit?

39
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:19,033
After the decision, never inside it.

40
00:02:19,033 --> 00:02:23,200
It reads each sealed artifact and explains it in plain English,

41
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:27,200
and every number it writes is checked against that artifact.

42
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:30,867
Invent one and the explanation is rejected and counted.

43
00:02:30,867 --> 00:02:33,300
So far: 238 explained, 0 rejected.

44
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:34,367
Live, so far:

45
00:02:34,367 --> 00:02:38,400
minus 565 dollars and 7 cents on a hundred thousand dollar paper account.

46
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,767
Four condors open, twenty eight contracts,

47
00:02:40,767 --> 00:02:44,367
three thousand one hundred and eight dollars of credit collected,

48
00:02:44,367 --> 00:02:48,167
against a worst case capped at ten thousand eight hundred and forty.

49
00:02:48,167 --> 00:02:50,500
The tail hedge is coded and never engaged:

50
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:53,400
no VIX expiry inside its window was quoted all week.

51
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:57,933
In ninety minutes the agent flattens the book and that number becomes realised.

52
00:02:58,233 --> 00:02:59,833
Clone it. Run make judge.

53
00:02:59,833 --> 00:03:01,633
You do not have to trust me.

54
00:03:01,633 --> 00:03:04,367
That is the whole design.
